   player. Safari composites that cheaply; Gecko repaints every tile under the video each frame and so
   never reaches macOS's low-power ("detached") video mode. Hiding it (exp 006, chip power):
     1080p24 fullscreen 0.32 -> 0.11 W (Safari 0.19), GPU -> 0
     1080p60 fullscreen 0.36 -> 0.14 W (Safari 0.29)
     1080p60 windowed   0.53 -> 0.26 W (Safari 0.59)
   Visible cost: no coloured glow around the player / in the letterbox bars.
   Equivalent without CSS: YouTube player Settings (gear) -> Ambient mode -> off, in each browser. */
@-moz-document domain(youtube.com) {
  #cinematics-container, #cinematics { display: none !important; }
}

prefs._userChrome:
/* Make Firefox Great Again: Zen power fixes that need CSS (no pref exists).
   Requires toolkit.legacyUserProfileCustomizations.stylesheets = true (set in user.js). */

/* The sidebar media card plays an animated music-note sprite (30 steps/s, forever) while any tab
   has audio, even when compact mode hides the sidebar. YouTube audio in a background tab:
   chip 0.21 W -> 0.07 W, WindowServer 264 -> 12 ms/s (experiment 005). The media card and its
   buttons stay; only the dancing notes go. */
.zen-media-notes { display: none !important; }

